name: agent-teams
description: Auto-spawn Codex agent teams (experimental) for parallel coordinated work on a shared codebase. Use when task is complex, read-heavy, spans multiple layers (security + API + frontend), needs parallel hypothesis testing, or touches a large codebase (>15 files / >50K lines). Team lead breaks work into subtasks, spawns teammates via TeamCreate, teammates coordinate via shared task list + peer-to-peer mailbox. Picks roles from installed agents in ~/.Codex/agents/ (engineering, design, testing, product, marketing). Triggers on "spawn a team", "agent team", "parallel agents", "multi-agent review", "team of agents", large refactors, full-codebase analysis, multi-layer code review.
